item.description:
This step runs in the borrower's browser, so there is no API request to send here.

1. Allow Truv in your Content Security Policy. A missing policy is a common reason the widget does not load.
   - script-src: cdn.truv.com
   - frame-src: my.truv.com, cdn.truv.com, prod.truv.com
2. Load the script: https://cdn.truv.com/bridge.js
3. Pass the bridge_token from Create order (your backend hands it to the page):

   const bridge = TruvBridge.init({
     bridgeToken: BRIDGE_TOKEN,
     isOrder: true,
     onLoad: () => {},
     onSuccess: () => {},
     onClose: () => {},
     onEvent: (type, payload, source) => {
       if (type === 'COMPLETED' && source === 'order') { /* advance the application */ }
     }
   });
   bridge.open();

4. Advance the borrower only when onEvent reports COMPLETED from the order source. Do not advance on onSuccess or onClose, because connections can still be pending at that point.
5. Enable your "Verify income" button right after TruvBridge.init returns, and call bridge.open() on click. Do not wait for onLoad: with isOrder: true, onLoad only fires after open(), so a button gated on onLoad never becomes clickable.
6. The widget opens as a centered dialog by default. Inline embedding is described on Truv's Display Modes page.

Sandbox login in Bridge: search for Truv Payroll Provider, then use goodlogin / goodpassword (full-time current employment). Other sandbox usernames cover hourly part-time (hourly.part-time) and multiple employers (multiple.employments), both with goodpassword.

Any sandbox payroll provider accepts these logins, for example ADP, not only Truv Payroll Provider. When the sandbox asks for an MFA code, enter 12345.
